.TH SYSLOGCEF 1 "August 2026" "syslogcef 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
syslogcef \- convert syslog events to ArcSight Common Event Format (CEF)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B syslogcef
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] [\fIPATHS\fR...]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B syslogcef
converts syslog events into ArcSight Common Event Format (CEF) for
consumption by SIEM platforms. It automatically detects and parses
RFC3164 (BSD), RFC5424 (including structured data), rsyslog JSON and
file formats, and systemd journal exports (JSON, short, and ISO
formats).
.PP
Input is read from the given \fIPATHS\fR, or from standard input when no
paths are given. One CEF record is emitted per input line. Unparseable
lines never abort the stream; they fall back to a raw-message event.
.PP
Vendor/product mappings for Cisco ASA, Cisco IOS, F5 BIG-IP, generic
Linux, and VMware ESXi are bundled and selected automatically from
message content; custom mappings can be supplied as JSON files.
Log content is treated as untrusted input: CEF header and extension
values are escaped so crafted messages cannot forge header fields or
split records.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BR \-o ", " \-\-output " \fIFILE\fR"
Write CEF lines to \fIFILE\fR instead of standard output.
.TP
.BR \-a ", " \-\-append
Append to the output file instead of truncating it.
.TP
.BR \-\-mode " \fIMODE\fR"
Force a specific parser instead of auto-detection. One of
.BR rfc3164 ,
.BR rfc5424 ,
.BR rsyslog_json ,
.BR rsyslog_file ,
.BR journald_json ,
.BR journald_short ,
.BR journald_iso .
.TP
.BR \-\-mapping " \fIFILE\fR"
Use the mapping JSON file \fIFILE\fR. When omitted, a bundled mapping is
selected automatically from message content.
.TP
.B \-\-tail
Follow the input files like
.BR "tail \-f" ;
all given files are tailed concurrently.
.TP
.B \-\-multiprocess
Convert lines using a process pool.
.TP
.BR \-\-pool\-size " \fIN\fR"
Number of worker processes for
.BR \-\-multiprocess
(default: CPU count minus one).
.TP
.BR \-\-log\-level " \fILEVEL\fR"
Python logging level (default
.BR WARNING ).
.SH EXAMPLES
Convert a log file to CEF on standard output:
.PP
.nf
.RS
syslogcef < /var/log/syslog
.RE
.fi
.PP
Follow two files in real time and append CEF to an output file:
.PP
.nf
.RS
syslogcef /var/log/asa.log /var/log/messages \-\-tail \-\-append \-o events.cef
.RE
.fi
.PP
Force the Cisco ASA mapping:
.PP
.nf
.RS
syslogcef asa.log \-\-mapping /usr/share/syslogcef/mappings/cisco_asa.json
.RE
.fi
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /etc/syslogcef/syslogcef.conf
Configuration for the system service: input file, output file, and
extra arguments.
.TP
.I syslogcef.service
systemd unit (RPM and Debian packages) that follows the configured
input and appends CEF to the configured output. On Alpine the
equivalent OpenRC service is configured via
.IR /etc/conf.d/syslogcef .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.B syslogcef
exits 0 on success and non-zero if input files cannot be read or
arguments are invalid.
.SH SEE ALSO
Project homepage and issue tracker:
.UR https://github.com/allamiro/syslogcef
.UE
